    baslik: Is therapy for everyone?
    metin: |-
      Short answer: Yes. The belief that therapy is only for people with "serious" mental health problems is common but mistaken. Therapy is also a valuable tool for developing self-awareness, breaking recurring patterns, improving relationships or getting support through a difficult period.

      That said, some signs may be pointing to "now is the time." If you are unsure how the process works, our guide to [psychological support in North Cyprus](/en/blog/psychological-support-north-cyprus.html) is a good starting point.
  - type: ozel
    html: |-
      <div>
                  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-6">7 important signs</h2>
                  <div class="space-y-4">

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">1</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Emotional distress is affecting daily life</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">If <a href="/en/blog/what-is-anxiety-disorder.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">anxiety</a>, sadness, anger or hopelessness is negatively affecting your work, relationships or daily functioning, it is time for an assessment.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">2</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">You notice recurring patterns</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">"Why does the same thing keep happening in every relationship?" or "Why do I keep falling into the same trap?" are excellent starting points for deeper exploration.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">3</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Noticeable changes in sleep, appetite or energy</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Persistent fatigue, insomnia or oversleeping, changes in appetite — these can be signals that the body is carrying stress or emotional burden.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">4</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">Your coping strategies are causing harm</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Coping mechanisms such as alcohol, overeating, excessive social media use or avoidance may provide short-term relief but can make the problem worse over time.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">5</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">You have experienced a trauma or loss</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Seeking support after major life events such as bereavement, separation, accident, job loss or fertility difficulties can significantly speed up the healing process.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-2xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">6</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">You feel isolated</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Withdrawing from others, not wanting to be a burden, or the feeling that "nobody understands" — these are things you can safely explore in a therapy setting.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex gap-4 bg-accent/8 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-accent/20">
                      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-accent text-white font-serif font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">7</div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">You simply want to grow and understand yourself better</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Therapy is not only for crises. It can be started to increase self-awareness, clarify goals or build more fulfilling relationships. This is a decision that comes from strength.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                  </div>
